WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Flip on a light.

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.800
Somewhere, a coal power plant just
sold a little more electricity.

3
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.390
The plant pays for its fuel,

4
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.560
its workers and its equipment.

5
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.380
You pay your electric bill.

6
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.840
Everyone settles up.

7
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.590
Supply meets demand, and
the market looks like it

8
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.110
is working exactly as it should.

9
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.930
Yet economists say it produces too much.

10
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.300
So why does a factory
that pays all its own

11
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.890
bills still produce too much?

12
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.550
In this mission, you'll find
the socially optimal quantity,

13
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:33.480
where marginal social benefit
equals marginal social cost.

14
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.380
Then you'll calculate the deadweight
loss when the market misses it.

15
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.560
Your mission: find out
what the market leaves out,

16
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.190
and what it costs society.
